Enough. I value your opinion, Tara, but that does not allow you to question my commands.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.850
They'll send some soldiers to meet us.

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:37.600
I'm afraid they'll want to blindfold you.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.560
It's just a security precaution.

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:42.650
Thank you for the reassurance.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:46.490
Now, if you don't mind, I'll need a few moments of silence to prepare myself.

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:48.930
Of course.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.170
I can't pinpoint the source.

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.110
We're still within their jamming range.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.970
I suggest we cancel the negotiations and return to your ship.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:11.510
For once, we're in full agreement.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:17.040
Direct hit to our starboard engine. Main power is offline.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.100
Now you see who you're dealing with, Captain?

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.420
If you don't mind, Ambassador.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:22.760
We're losing altitude. 200 meters.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.220
Gonna bring us in on thrusters.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.420
100 meters.

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:35.450
We need to reduce our speed the ground is gonna do that for us brace yourself

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:18.620
Any idea where we are the southeast quadrant near the old spaceport I told you I negotiated the last accord

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:29.890
I also served here you were with the occupation force as an intelligence officer a long time ago our current deployment has a base of

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.760
operations that way, about two and a half kilometers.

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:34.940
I appreciate your help, Ambassador,

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:36.300
but we're looking for the Andorians.

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:40.660
Circumstances have altered our plans.

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:43.410
I gave my word to Shran, I intend to keep it.

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:47.480
Shran just tried to kill us.

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:49.540
We don't know that.

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:53.000
I suppose you think our troops are responsible for this.

00:22:53.380 --> 00:22:55.100
Sensors and communications are offline.

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:57.500
There's weapons fire flying all over the place.

00:22:57.640 --> 00:22:58.760
We don't know what happened.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:22:59.900
Are you?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:00.640
That naive.

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:02.790
Shran is using you.

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:04.740
This is a man who couldn't sleep

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:06.200
because he thought he owed me something.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:09.380
I don't believe he asked me to come a dozen light years

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:11.220
just so I could lead you into a trap.

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:16.980
Right now, it seems like the best thing to do

00:23:16.980 --> 00:23:18.860
is to get a ceasefire in place.

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:20.890
The Andorians won't agree to that

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:22.770
until they talk to you in person.

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:25.800
I managed to keep us on course most of the way in.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.880
We can't be more than a kilometer

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.060
from Shran's landing coordinates.

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:43.140
How would you know?

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:45.330
We can't pick up anything through the interference.

00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:47.980
Our scanners are more sophisticated than yours.

00:23:48.380 --> 00:23:50.680
We detected weapons fire coming from the surface.

00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:53.600
Then your shuttle appeared to make an emergency landing

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:54.640
somewhere in the colony.

00:23:55.790 --> 00:23:56.050
Where?

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:58.710
We haven't been able to pinpoint their landing site,

00:23:58.850 --> 00:23:59.970
but our units on the ground are-

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:03.870
already searching. The high command instructed me to take steps to recover

00:24:03.870 --> 00:24:04.890
ambassadors of all.

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:09.720
There are officers? Of course. We want to be involved in any rescue operation.

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:16.380
We have more experience in these matters. I know. I once saw one of your commando

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:19.360
units blast the hell out of a rebel compound during a rescue mission.

00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:23.680
We won't allow this provocation to continue. You don't even know where they

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:23.920
are.

00:24:24.740 --> 00:24:28.250
Do you really think it's a good idea to go down there guns blazing? Our response

00:24:28.250 --> 00:24:28.970
will be appropriate.

00:24:30.250 --> 00:24:32.020
I'll keep you informed, Commander.

00:24:36.340 --> 00:24:36.720
Any luck?

00:24:36.980 --> 00:24:37.820
I'm trying, sir.

00:24:38.200 --> 00:24:39.880
But if the Vulcans can't find him...

00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:41.450
See what you can do?

00:24:41.950 --> 00:24:42.270
Yes, sir.

00:24:44.380 --> 00:24:45.780
Fire away of those Endorian ships.

00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:48.560
Three hours at their present speed.

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:56.160
The shuttle was to be left alone.

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:57.680
I gave specific orders.

00:24:57.820 --> 00:24:58.880
And they were followed.

00:24:59.040 --> 00:24:59.940
Then who fired those shots?

00:25:00.280 --> 00:25:02.940
Vulcans, I suppose, trying to kill their own ambassador.

00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:04.120
That's so unlikely.

00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:06.660
Some of my men saw weapons fire coming from their positions.

00:25:07.940 --> 00:25:09.840
Vulcan subterfuge, I'm sure of it.

00:25:10.180 --> 00:25:12.160
What better way for them to justify an invasion

00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:14.020
than to blame us for killing their envoy?

00:25:14.560 --> 00:25:16.980
They are devious, but I doubt even they would go that far.

00:25:17.970 --> 00:25:19.650
It's as if they have some moral code.

00:25:19.890 --> 00:25:21.250
They have no conscience.

00:25:21.550 --> 00:25:22.970
Only their precious logic.

00:25:23.090 --> 00:25:25.010
They'll do anything to drive us off this planet.

00:25:25.190 --> 00:25:27.030
We should never have agreed to negotiate.

00:25:28.420 --> 00:25:29.980
You're not happy with the way I...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:38.450
handled this situation of course i am sir the sector two reports sir put our positions on alert

00:25:38.450 --> 00:25:43.680
i want savall and the pink skin brought to me alive if they're looking for an excuse to attack

00:25:43.680 --> 00:25:46.350
we won't give it to them i'll see to it myself

00:26:03.290 --> 00:26:05.390
Perhaps you were farther off course than you thought.

00:26:05.940 --> 00:26:07.960
You've been here before. I don't suppose you'd care to help.

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:09.860
It's been almost a hundred years.

00:26:10.120 --> 00:26:11.830
I thought Vulcans had exceptional memories.

00:26:14.270 --> 00:26:15.870
This is the old residential quarter.

00:26:17.050 --> 00:26:18.490
According to our latest intelligence,

00:26:18.850 --> 00:26:21.110
the Andorians control the settlement west of here.

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:25.920
Moving this way, we should be...

00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:26.260
Down!

00:26:33.770 --> 00:26:35.930
Not quite the warm welcome you expected, Captain.

00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:49.940
Units must be advancing their positions.

00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:51.710
We should try to make contact with him.

00:26:52.130 --> 00:26:53.870
I don't recommend sticking your neck out right now.

00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:55.540
What do you recommend?

00:26:56.080 --> 00:26:58.280
Wandering through these ruins until we find an Andorian

00:26:58.280 --> 00:26:59.900
soldier and trust he's been informed.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:16.460
to shoot us on sight captain that's an order no offense but my ears are less likely to draw fire

00:27:16.460 --> 00:27:24.500
than yours what is their fixation with our ears i believe they're envious do you realize you picked

00:27:24.500 --> 00:27:29.960
up a slight human accent you're one of the most promising members of my staff to paul

00:27:31.050 --> 00:27:33.770
If you'd stayed in San Francisco, you'd be the assistant counsel by now.

00:27:34.380 --> 00:27:36.660
You might even have a diplomatic posting of your own.

00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:37.780
I'm aware of that.

00:27:39.020 --> 00:27:40.500
Then why have you remained on Enterprise?

00:27:41.240 --> 00:27:44.180
We believed they needed our help when they first developed warp drive.

00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:45.260
That hasn't changed.

00:27:46.180 --> 00:27:48.280
Captain Archer's record is evidence of that.

00:27:48.420 --> 00:27:50.070
But there are others who can assist them.

00:27:52.200 --> 00:27:53.640
I find the work gratifying.

00:27:56.960 --> 00:27:59.240
Gratification is an emotional indulgence.

00:28:00.470 --> 00:28:01.810
You disagreed with our recommendation

00:28:01.810 --> 00:28:04.690
that Archer's mission be canceled after the tragedy

00:28:04.690 --> 00:28:05.490
at Paraga 2.

00:28:06.360 --> 00:28:06.680
Why?

00:28:07.510 --> 00:28:09.170
I was on board Enterprise at the time.

00:28:10.100 --> 00:28:11.620
I felt my opinion would be welcomed.

00:28:11.990 --> 00:28:13.650
You believed you knew better than the high command?

00:28:14.520 --> 00:28:16.420
That sounds a great deal like another emotion.

00:28:17.080 --> 00:28:17.440
arrogance

00:28:19.190 --> 00:28:21.390
Perhaps it's time for you to consider another assignment.

00:28:25.180 --> 00:28:29.840
Just because Captain Archer has earned my respect doesn't mean I've been contaminated by his emotions.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.980
We'll be right back.

00:28:34.280 --> 00:28:34.980
Did you make contact?

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:36.040
No.

00:28:36.870 --> 00:28:37.430
They're pulling back.

00:28:38.060 --> 00:28:38.540
Let's keep moving.

00:28:46.020 --> 00:28:46.380
Empty.

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:48.780
They're probably trying to reach the Hawkins.

00:28:49.900 --> 00:28:50.220
No.

00:28:50.790 --> 00:28:52.970
The pinkskin will want to keep his part of the bargain.

00:28:54.120 --> 00:28:55.380
They'll be looking for Shran.

00:29:02.230 --> 00:29:02.570
Commander.

00:29:03.130 --> 00:29:03.690
You have something?

00:29:05.300 --> 00:29:06.020
I can't be sure.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.360
You see this EM differential here?

00:29:09.270 --> 00:29:09.890
Back to Cap'n.

00:29:10.420 --> 00:29:13.500
It's definitely a biosign. I'm 90% sure it's human.

00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:14.820
At least we know he's alive.

00:29:15.420 --> 00:29:15.860
Where is he?

00:29:16.380 --> 00:29:17.220
I need another hour.

00:29:19.420 --> 00:29:20.940
What's the status on those Andorian ships?

00:29:21.690 --> 00:29:22.750
They just dropped out of four.

00:29:23.770 --> 00:29:25.010
He'll be here in 13 minutes.

00:29:26.100 --> 00:29:27.280
I think the Valkans see them too.

00:29:27.770 --> 00:29:28.490
They're breaking orbit.

00:29:29.140 --> 00:29:29.840
probably giving themselves

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:30.620
There's room to manoeuvre.

00:29:31.460 --> 00:29:32.620
Put the ship on tactical alert.

00:29:47.300 --> 00:29:47.640
Get down.

00:30:15.930 --> 00:30:17.050
Those are Andorian weapons.

00:30:23.580 --> 00:30:23.900
How is he?

00:30:25.720 --> 00:30:26.760
It isn't life-threatening.

00:30:27.640 --> 00:30:28.760
but he needs medical attention.

00:30:29.270 --> 00:30:29.550
Thank you.

00:30:32.330 --> 00:30:32.870
We've brought-

00:30:33.450 --> 00:30:34.910
Master to meet with Commander Shran!

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:38.480
Looks like two of them.

00:30:40.200 --> 00:30:41.480
One on top of that structure.

00:30:43.720 --> 00:30:44.320
Neither on the ground.

00:30:49.800 --> 00:30:50.680
See if I can work my way around.

00:30:52.870 --> 00:30:54.050
Some of my people are coming from behind them.

00:30:56.780 --> 00:30:57.680
What do you expect me to do with this?

00:30:58.220 --> 00:30:59.220
Make sure they don't see me.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.600
I haven't fired a weapon in 50 years.

00:31:01.720 --> 00:31:02.640
You don't have to hit anything.

00:31:02.970 --> 00:31:03.950
Just keep them occupied.

00:31:06.940 --> 00:31:08.000
Really Occupied.

00:31:08.630 --> 00:31:09.830
or I'm not going to get very far.

00:31:30.220 --> 00:31:30.340
Thank you.

00:32:13.820 --> 00:32:23.130
A thousand kilometers still heading right for the Vulcan ships the Vulcans are charging weapons and Dorians as well Travis Lane a new course

00:32:23.130 --> 00:32:29.580
I want you to put us right between them. Hi, sir. If you don't mind me asking

00:32:30.700 --> 00:32:31.500
What do you have in mind?

00:33:15.070 --> 00:33:21.040
I've never fired one of these before.

00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:23.850
I'm sure if it's set on stun.

00:33:26.980 --> 00:33:27.960
False, fire!

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.060
It doesn't have a stunned setting.

00:33:38.500 --> 00:33:39.300
Fire on my shuttle.

00:33:40.340 --> 00:33:41.600
You're trying to kill Saval.

00:33:42.540 --> 00:33:44.640
Undermine everything that Shran is trying to do here.

00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:45.000
Why?

00:33:46.950 --> 00:33:48.250
Do you want a war with the Vulcans?

00:33:49.270 --> 00:33:51.990
All we want is a chance to fight for what's ours

00:33:51.990 --> 00:33:56.270
before cowards like Shran negotiate it away.

00:33:57.350 --> 00:33:58.470
You can take that up with him.

00:34:00.670 --> 00:34:01.050
Let's go.

00:35:02.400 --> 00:35:06.840
We're being hailed by the Vulcans and the Andorians.

00:35:07.590 --> 00:35:08.310
We're both on.

00:35:10.580 --> 00:35:11.620
This is Commander Tucker.

00:35:12.590 --> 00:35:14.430
Captain Teller of the Imperial Guard.

00:35:14.610 --> 00:35:17.650
Commander, I strongly recommend you withdraw to a safe distance.

00:35:17.950 --> 00:35:18.410
I agree.

00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:22.670
We want your vessel to be damaged by debris from the Vulcan ships.

00:35:22.830 --> 00:35:26.470
We will not allow the Andorians to land additional troops on Pan Makar.

00:35:26.670 --> 00:35:29.970
It's called Weitan, and our personnel there have been attacked.

00:35:30.160 --> 00:35:37.500
We'll provide whatever support they need any vessel attempting to enter orbit will be fired upon that includes your sub commander

00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:46.440
We appreciate your support commander Tucker. Don't I'll open fire on any ship that makes an aggressive move face cannons

00:35:47.680 --> 00:35:54.400
Locked and ready. This is not a star fleet matter as long as my captain is stuck in the middle of your war zone

00:35:54.400 --> 00:35:59.970
It is the Endorians have made it impossible for us to recover Captain Archer by now

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:06.960
he's most likely a casualty don't count him out so fast we've managed to isolate his bio signature

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:19.280
now why don't you both give him and ambassador soval a chance to do their jobs before we start

00:36:19.280 --> 00:36:26.400
a war up here he was ready to kill me you saw for yourself apparently these pink skins aren't as

00:36:26.400 --> 00:36:27.600
honorable as you thought

00:36:32.200 --> 00:36:41.140
Are you all right? I suppose I shot the ambassador to make my story more convincing.

00:36:42.910 --> 00:36:47.140
Why would my lieutenant, a loyal member of the Imperial Guard, lie to me?

00:36:48.140 --> 00:36:52.760
Commander, it seems you're willing to resolve this situation through peaceful means.

00:36:53.620 --> 00:36:55.680
Do all your officers feel the same?

00:36:57.640 --> 00:36:59.860
Have you considered there might be Andorians?

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.220
who would want a war with Vulcan.

00:37:07.380 --> 00:37:09.000
Have I served with you?

00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:12.980
Followed your orders when it could have meant my life?

00:37:13.890 --> 00:37:15.590
She's not the only one who risked their life.

00:37:18.170 --> 00:37:19.630
I said I'd bring Soval to meet you,

00:37:19.690 --> 00:37:21.410
and we damn near got killed getting him here.

00:37:23.580 --> 00:37:24.800
It came because you asked me,

00:37:25.980 --> 00:37:27.140
because you thought I could be trusted.

00:37:28.740 --> 00:37:29.520
Check Soval's wound.

00:37:30.760 --> 00:37:34.170
Check our shuttle. You'll find Andorian weapon signatures.

00:37:44.610 --> 00:37:49.050
This is true. Answer me!

00:37:50.690 --> 00:37:52.170
What did you expect me to do?

00:37:52.700 --> 00:37:54.360
Follow my orders!

00:37:55.350 --> 00:37:58.590
Orders to do nothing while you betray us.

00:37:58.710 --> 00:37:59.970
It's not...

00:38:00.030 --> 00:38:16.400
late to redeem yourself to make a stand i intend to there are others who feel this way you'll see

00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:29.870
see to the ambassador's wounds we have a lot to

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:41.440
discuss. The Vulcan ships are breaking formation. They're heading for the planet. The Andorians are

00:38:41.440 --> 00:38:46.470
following, sir. Arm the forward face cannons. See if you can target their weapons. We're being hailed

00:38:46.470 --> 00:38:55.040
from the surface, Captain. Hold off, Malcolm. Put him through. Captain! Nice to hear your voice, Trip.

00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:59.980
What's going on down there? You okay? Paul and I are fine.

00:39:00.570 --> 00:39:02.010
at the Andorian command post.

00:39:02.540 --> 00:39:04.180
Ambassador Saval's been injured,

00:39:04.380 --> 00:39:05.960
but Shran's medics are treating him.

00:39:06.420 --> 00:39:07.860
Did you say Shran's medics?

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:09.400
He's just being a good host.

00:39:10.020 --> 00:39:12.020
The Andorians are allowing the Vulcan ships

00:39:12.020 --> 00:39:13.520
to move in and pick up their people.

00:39:14.260 --> 00:39:15.180
Glad you let us know.

00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:17.820
Did you run into any problems up there?

00:39:19.860 --> 00:39:20.740
Nothing we couldn't handle.

00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:22.340
I'll fill you in later.

00:39:22.890 --> 00:39:24.350
We had a pretty rough landing.

00:39:24.600 --> 00:39:25.720
We'll need a ride back to the ship.

00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:27.840
I'll send Travis down and settle pod two.

00:39:28.510 --> 00:39:28.910
Acknowledged.

00:39:29.310 --> 00:39:29.770
Archer out.

00:39:31.790 --> 00:39:35.580
Put us back in orbit, Travis, and cancel the tactical alert.

00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:40.040
Captain Starlog supplemental.

00:39:40.920 --> 00:39:43.660
Ambassador Saval has begun talks with the Andorians.

00:39:44.230 --> 00:39:47.060
They've been difficult, but productive.

00:39:48.100 --> 00:39:50.750
Imperial Council will not be satisfied

00:39:50.750 --> 00:39:54.400
until Vulcan recognizes our claim to wait on.

00:39:56.090 --> 00:39:59.970
I believe someone wants to find a compromise as a solution.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.640
that neither side is happy with.

00:40:02.870 --> 00:40:05.810
In that case, these talks have been extremely successful.

00:40:06.360 --> 00:40:09.720
I consider any negotiation that averts war to be a success.

00:40:16.310 --> 00:40:16.670
Join me.

00:40:18.490 --> 00:40:18.810
Drink.

00:40:19.730 --> 00:40:20.350
to celebrate.

00:40:21.820 --> 00:40:23.660
our mutual dissatisfaction.

00:40:25.180 --> 00:40:26.200
Vulcans don't drink.

00:40:31.340 --> 00:40:33.580
But this occasion merits an exception.

00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:44.320
to the ceasefire.

00:40:45.420 --> 00:40:48.320
It wouldn't have been possible without the help of our human friends.

00:40:49.260 --> 00:40:53.120
and to the successful continuation of these talks on Andoria.

00:40:54.410 --> 00:40:56.590
Trust they'll be more accomplished than just.

00:40:57.220 --> 00:40:57.520
talk.

00:41:12.630 --> 00:41:15.570
With your permission, I'll escort Ambassador Sebal to the airlock.

00:41:16.570 --> 00:41:16.850
Of course.

00:41:26.490 --> 00:41:27.510
Your presence here.

00:41:28.280 --> 00:41:28.700
It's not.

00:41:28.950 --> 00:41:29.270
Ben

00:41:30.730 --> 00:41:31.790
overly meddlesome

00:41:46.860 --> 00:41:48.400
I think he likes you, pink skin.

00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:51.580
would
